# Copy to .env and fill in. NEVER commit the real .env (it's gitignored).

NODE_ENV=production

# First-run admin (seeded once, on an empty database).
ADMIN_EMAIL=you@example.com
# Use a long, random password. In production the app refuses to start if this
# is missing, still "changeme", or shorter than 10 characters.
ADMIN_PASSWORD=change-me-to-a-long-random-secret

# Cloudflare Tunnel token: Zero Trust dashboard → Networks → Tunnels →
# (your tunnel) → install connector → copy the token from the docker command.
# In the tunnel's Public Hostname config, point your hostname at:  http://web:8787
# Anyone holding this token can run a connector on your hostname — keep it in
# .env only, and rotate it in the dashboard if it ever lands somewhere shared.
TUNNEL_TOKEN=paste-your-tunnel-token-here

# ---- optional overrides ----
# PORT=8787
# TRUST_PROXY=1
# COOKIE_SECURE=true
# SESSION_MAX_AGE_DAYS=30
# MIN_PASSWORD_LENGTH=8
# Chromecast media-token signing secret. Defaults to a random per-boot value
# (restarts interrupt in-flight casts); set a long random string to make
# tokens survive restarts. Not needed for normal local/browser playback.
# CAST_TOKEN_SECRET=

# ---- Debrid backends (the quality tier — all playback) ----
# Movies and TV resolve a torrent release through a debrid service. Backends are
# tried IN ORDER and are fully independent: one being down, rate-limited or
# simply not holding a release just moves on to the next. At least one is
# required for the Movies/TV tabs to appear at all.
#
# Real-Debrid — https://real-debrid.com/apitoken
# REAL_DEBRID_TOKEN=
#
# Premiumize (optional, recommended) — https://www.premiumize.me/account
# A SECOND cache to ask when Real-Debrid hasn't got a release: different service,
# different library, so a title missing from one often plays from the other.
# It also supports a bulk cache lookup, which RD retired — one request tells the
# app which of a film's ~100 releases are playable, so it picks the best cached
# one instead of discovering it by trial and error.
# PREMIUMIZE_API_KEY=

# ---- VidLink (FLOOR tier for Movies and TV) ----
# Without this, a title Real-Debrid hasn't cached means waiting while RD pulls
# it off the swarm. This answers in about a second with a direct MP4 — no index,
# no seeders, no debrid call — and never outranks a real release file.
#
# Movies and TV only. Anime has no floor source at all since Seanime was removed
# (2026-08-06), and VidLink cannot take its place: measured, it has no
# current-season episodes, which is the whole point of that vertical.
#
# READ THIS BEFORE ENABLING. VidLink's API is authorised by a token produced by
# a ~2.4 MB Go/WebAssembly binary they compile and serve; there is no id-only
# endpoint. Using this source therefore means running their code on your NAS.
# It is mitigated, not eliminated:
#   • the binary runs on a worker thread inside a stripped sandbox with no
#     fetch, no fs, no process and no require (lib/providers/vidlink/worker.mjs)
#   • its only real capability is one crypto primitive we hand it
#   • both assets are pinned by SHA-256 on first download, and a later change
#     FAILS CLOSED rather than executing — re-pinning is deliberate
# That is defence in depth, not a guarantee, which is why it ships off.
# VIDLINK=false
#
# Pins are written to <data>/vidlink/pins.json on first use. To accept a
# rebuild, delete that directory, or set the new digests here.
# VIDLINK_PIN_WASM=
# VIDLINK_PIN_GLUE=
# VIDLINK_TIMEOUT_MS=12000
#
# ---- the no-ads lock ----
# Extracting server-side already removes every ad on their page: Adcash and
# PopAds live in JavaScript we never load. The only remaining way an ad reaches
# a viewer is server-side insertion, and that needs a PLAYLIST to splice
# segments into — a progressive MP4 is one static file with nowhere to put one.
# So MP4 is all this accepts, and HLS is refused outright.
#
# Setting this to true opts back in. Even then every playlist is fetched and
# scanned for splice markers (CUE-OUT, SCTE35, DISCONTINUITY) and dropped if any
# are present, and a playlist that cannot be read is treated as NOT clean — the
# check fails closed, because a floor stream is optional and an ad is not.
# Leave it alone unless you have a reason.
# VIDLINK_ALLOW_HLS=false
#
# ---- make it the PRIMARY source for Movies and TV ----
# Normally the floor tier only runs when Real-Debrid has nothing cached. This
# inverts that: play the free, instant stream first and treat the debrid release
# as the upgrade. Worth trying if RD's cost, cache misses and outages buy you
# nothing you actually watch — the ceiling is a ~1080p MP4, so no REMUX, no 4K,
# no HDR, no lossless audio.
#
# Anime is deliberately unaffected: VidLink has no current-season episodes
# (measured — Frieren S1 plays, S2 returns nothing), and airing simulcasts are
# the whole point of that vertical.
#
# Picking a release by hand in the Servers panel always overrides this.
# VIDLINK_PRIMARY=false

# Send every stream through this server instead of straight from the debrid CDN.
# Slower (all video crosses your uplink) but hides members' IPs from the service.
# RD_DIRECT=false
# Movies/TV catalogs and torrent discovery ride the public Stremio addons
# (keyless). Override only to point at a mirror or self-hosted instance.
# CINEMETA_BASE=https://v3-cinemeta.strem.io
# TORRENTIO_BASE=https://torrentio.strem.fun
# RELATIONS_BASE=https://relations.yuna.moe

# ---- extra release sources for Movies and TV ----
# Torrentio scrapes many indexers but is ONE hosted service, and the only
# fallback behind it is apibay, which is one site. Any number of additional
# Stremio-protocol addons can be listed here, comma-separated; each is queried
# beside Torrentio and merged, and each fails independently.
#
# This is configuration rather than code on purpose — these services churn, so
# a dead one should be a URL swap, not a release.
#
# Most addons bake per-user settings into the PATH, so paste whatever their web
# UI gives you, config segment and all. A pasted .../manifest.json is fixed up
# automatically. Unset = disabled, and nothing else changes.
# STREMIO_ADDONS=https://mediafusion.elfhosted.com/D-aBc.../,https://comet.elfhosted.com/cfg.../

# ---- providers ----
# Sources are tiered (see lib/providers/index.mjs):
#   quality — debrid-backed releases. Ranked on picture and sound alone, and
#             the only tier that can deliver REMUX / 4K / lossless 5.1.
#   floor   — streaming sites. Low bitrate by construction (those hosts store
#             1-2 GB per title), so they exist purely so something plays
#             instantly while the quality release is acquired. Never
#             load-bearing. MOVIES AND TV ONLY — see the VidLink section above.
#             Anime has no floor source: its plays wait for the release.

# ---- ranking ----
# The floor the ranker refuses to go below. Releases under this resolution, and
# releases whose size-over-runtime says they are heavy re-encodes regardless of
# what the name claims, are dropped rather than ranked low.
# MIN_RESOLUTION=1080

# ---- source cache ----
# An LRU working set on the array, NOT a library — it self-evicts at the budget.
# Playback reads from here instead of re-pulling from the debrid CDN each watch,
# which is also what makes seeking and local transcoding reliable.
# Default is 5 TB of the 20 TB array. Raising it is the cheapest availability
# win there is: an evicted release has to be re-acquired from the swarm, and a
# resident one plays instantly no matter how few seeders it has left.
# CACHE_DIR=/media/cache
# CACHE_BUDGET_BYTES=5497558138880

# ---- transcoding ----
# LAN clients get the original bytes (remux at most). Remote clients get a
# capped encode sized for the tunnel — measured ceiling there is 9-26 Mbit/s
# against the residential upload leg, so 6 Mbit/s leaves headroom.
# Requires ffmpeg with QuickSync and /dev/dri passed into the container;
# verify with `vainfo` before trusting it.
# TRANSCODE=true
# TRANSCODE_HWACCEL=qsv
# TRANSCODE_REMOTE_MBPS=6
# TRANSCODE_MAX_SESSIONS=2

# Which audio track a FILM or live-action episode gets when the viewer hasn't
# picked one. Anime says sub/dub; everything else said nothing, and "nothing"
# meant the planner fell back on channel count — so a MULTi release carrying
# Spanish 5.1 and English 2.0 played Spanish for everyone. ISO-639-2/1 codes,
# best first. It's a preference, not a filter: a French film with no English
# track still plays its own audio. Empty string restores channels-first.
# AUDIO_LANGS=eng,en

# ---- LAN delivery ----
# The port a client reaches the app on IS the locality signal: behind
# cloudflared, req.ip is the tunnel's and can't distinguish a living-room TV
# from someone on hotel wifi. Set 0 to disable local delivery entirely.
# LAN_PORT=8788
